# http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C70663
<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C70663> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C70663> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C25364> .
<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C70663> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/NCIT" .
<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C70663> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Unique Identifier"@en .
<http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C70663> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A set of characters used as a code that is unique in the context or the system for which it is created. It serves as a means of identification and reference (often instead of a name) for an entity, person, thing, function, procedure, activity, variable, or body of data."@en .
