# 
# http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T001
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T072> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY" .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Organism"@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T001> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Generally, a living individual, including all plants and animals."@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T001> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> "Thesaurus:C14250 (http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C14250)" .
# 
# http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T002
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T002> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T204> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY" .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Plant"@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T002> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An organism having cellulose cell walls, growing by synthesis of inorganic substances, generally distinguished by the presence of chlorophyll, and lacking the power of locomotion. Plant parts are included here as well."@en .
# 
# http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T004
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T004> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T204> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY" .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fungus"@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T004> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A eukaryotic organism characterized by the absence of chlorophyll and the presence of a rigid cell wall. Included here are both slime molds and true fungi such as yeasts, molds, mildews, and mushrooms."@en .
# 
# http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T005
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T005> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T005> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T001> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T005> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY" .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T005> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Virus"@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T005> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An organism consisting of a core of a single nucleic acid enclosed in a protective coat of protein. A virus may replicate only inside a host living cell. A virus exhibits some but not all of the usual characteristics of living things."@en .
# 
# http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T007
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T007> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T001> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY" .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bacterium"@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T007> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A small, typically one-celled, prokaryotic micro-organism."@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T007> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#exactMatch> "Thesaurus:C14187 (http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C14187)" .
# 
# http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T008
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T008> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T008> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T204> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T008> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY" .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T008> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Animal"@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T008> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An organism with eukaryotic cells, and lacking stiff cell walls, plastids and photosynthetic pigments."@en .
# 
# http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T010
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T010> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T008> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY" .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Vertebrate"@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T010> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An animal which has a spinal column."@en .
# 
# http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T011
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T011> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T010> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY" .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Amphibian"@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T011> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A cold-blooded, smooth-skinned vertebrate which characteristically hatches as an aquatic larva, breathing by gills. When mature, the amphibian breathes with lungs."@en .
# 
# http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T012
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T012> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T012> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T010> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T012> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY" .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T012> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bird"@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T012> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A vertebrate having a constant body temperature and characterized by the presence of feathers."@en .
# 
# http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T013
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T013> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T013> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T010> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T013> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY" .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T013> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fish"@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T013> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A cold-blooded aquatic vertebrate characterized by fins and breathing by gills. Included here are fishes having either a bony skeleton, such as a perch, or a cartilaginous skeleton, such as a shark, or those lacking a jaw, such as a lamprey or hagfish."@en .
# 
# http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T014
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T014> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T014> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T010> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T014> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY" .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T014> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reptile"@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T014> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A cold-blooded vertebrate having an external covering of scales or horny plates. Reptiles breathe by means of lungs and are generally egg-laying."@en .
# 
# http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T015
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T015> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T015> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T010> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T015> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY" .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T015> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mammal"@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T015> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A vertebrate having a constant body temperature and characterized by the presence of hair, mammary glands and sweat glands."@en .
# 
# http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T051
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T051> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T051> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T051> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> "http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY" .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T051> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Event"@en .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T051> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A broad type for grouping activities, processes and states."@en .
# 
# http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/STY/T052
